  cites Mathbook chapter Simplify

 A Codex `Text` is a pointer to a four-byte length followed by CCE bytes, which
 a page cannot decode, so the module is a WASI program: the expression arrives
 on `fd_read` and the answer leaves on `fd_write`, both plain UTF-8 (R-CCE).

 `_start` runs once and exits, so the page instantiates the module per
 evaluation, and each evaluation gets a fresh heap.

Section: One Evaluation

 The simplifier's entry is `simplify`, which iterates to a fixed point under
 `simplify-fuel`; `fold-constants` is one pass at the TOP node only and answers
 `1 + 2 * 3` for `1+2*3`.

  mb-eval : Text -> Text
  mb-eval (line) =
    let parsed = parse-expr line
    in if parsed.po-ok
       then ex-print (simplify (parsed.po-expr))
       else "parse error: " & parsed.po-error

Section: Entry Point

  wasm-exports : Text = ""

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    entered <- read-line
    when entered
      is Just (line) -> print-line-uni (mb-eval line)
      is otherwise -> print-line-uni "parse error: no input"
    end
  end

